--- A1 (2026-09-08): endgame-phase frequency — NEGATIVE for
narrow endgame solving ---

From the banked 372k-decision harvest (free): only 4.9% of v10home
self-play hands ever reach stock <= 4; 1.4% reach stock <= 2; 0.8%
of decisions occur at stock <= 4. The home game is gin-dominated
and ends early. Even a +10 pts/hand solver inside the stock<=4
cell caps at ~0.5 pts/hand overall — below the gate noise floor.
Track A AS SPECCED (exact enumeration at stock <= 3-4) cannot pay
in match terms regardless of solver quality. The v6_prior_art §3
design rules remain valid for the cell; the cell is just too rare
in the home variant.

--- A2 REGISTRATION: oracle-gap phase decomposition ---

Instrument phase_oracle.py: HomeV8Policy machinery with the
belief's sampled worlds replaced by the TRUE opponent hidden hand
ONLY when stock <= K (world veto disabled in oracle phase);
otherwise the normal v10 particle posterior. Hero = phase-oracle,
opponent = v10home, paired-deal t10_gate harness, 1500 pairs per
K, seeds: K=99 -> 140000, K=10 -> 142000, K=4 -> 144000 (mod 977
= 289/335/381, distinct from all used).
  K=99 = the HOME oracle bound for v10home (never measured; the
  v8 log's open compass item). K=10 and K=4 give the marginal
  share of the gap that late-phase information alone captures.
Decision rule: if (K=4 margin) is within noise of zero, endgame
solving is DEAD for the home variant and the campaign pivots to
mid-game posterior consumption (design registered after the
decomposition is known). If the K=10..4 band carries >= 3
pts/hand, a raised-threshold solver (depth-limited) re-enters.

