--- V11b REFIT (2026-09-08, run during A2 dead time; extends the
v11 log's registered next step) ---

6th feature meldprot = VALUE[drop] + dw_after - dw_before (0 for
pure deadwood; large for meld members whose removal strands
partners). Held-out logloss unchanged vs 5-feat (meld-break states
are rare) but the weights REORGANIZE: value flips -0.30 -> ~+0.06
/ +0.10 while meldprot takes -0.40..-0.59 — the value weight had
been absorbing meld protection, which is the exact home10 failure
mechanism. 6-feat weights (open/pickup/draw):
  open   [-0.4916,-0.1405,-0.0938,-0.4998, 0.0,   -0.5854]
  pickup [-0.5002,-0.3089,+0.0995,-0.6517, 0.0,   -0.4007]
  draw   [-0.4882,-0.4722,+0.0557,-0.7255,+0.1375,-0.4325]
Integration + G-ladder re-entry queued behind the A2 oracle runs
(particle.py is imported by their workers — no edits until they
drain).

--- A2 RESULTS (2026-09-08): THE COMPASS CORRECTED ---

phase_oracle.py, 1500 paired deals per K (seeds 140000/142000/
144000):
  K=99 (full):      +15.25 +/- 1.92  <- the HOME oracle bound for
                                        v10home (first measurement)
  K=10:             +0.95 +/- 0.52
  K=4:              +0.29 +/- 0.25
VERDICTS:
1. ENDGAME SOLVING IS DEAD for the home variant (registered rule:
   K<=10 band 0.95 << 3). Track A as specced in v6_prior_art §3 is
   formally closed for home rules — the design rules stay valid
   for the standard game's longer endgames only.
2. >93% of the oracle bound lives at stock > 10 — the early/mid
   game. Much of that is IRREDUCIBLE hidden-information value (at
   turn 3 the observations do not determine the hand; the
   posterior checks showed the PF already captures 60-92% of the
   per-node information that IS there). The project's standing
   "~14 pts of belief headroom" framing overstated achievable
   headroom; the honest open question is the PERFECT-BELIEF bound
   (worlds from the exact Bayes conditional), which no cheap
   instrument currently measures.
3. K=10 oracle value +0.95 +/- 0.52 is real but sub-1-point — a
   ceiling on ANY late-phase improvement (belief or solver).
CAMPAIGN PIVOT (registered): v12 completes v11b (integration +
full G-ladder + the user-directed regression ladder) as its
deliverable; the strength frontier beyond that requires either a
perfect-belief-bound instrument or compute-scaling curves (the
v5-era anytime question) — to be registered separately.

